{"role":"assistant","content":"All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are implemented through the existing `Analytics` wrapper, and `ANSWER.md` documents the work.\n\n**Registration screen** (`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`)\n- `registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started` — fire once when the field first becomes non-empty, not per keystroke.\n- `loan_amount_changed` — fires on slider `onChangeEnd` with `{'amount': <int>}`; using `onChanged` would emit ~50 events per drag.\n- `terms_accepted` — fires only when the box is ticked, not unticked.\n- `registration_continue_tapped` — fires with `{'amount': <int>, 'terms': <bool>}` before navigating to `/offers`.\n\n**Offers screen** (`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`) — converted to `StatefulWidget` with a `ScrollController`; `offers_scrolled` fires once per visit when the list first scrolls past offset 0, with `{'offset': <double>}`.\n\nNo email/phone values are sent as properties, per the PII note, and no screen-view events were added (already handled by `PosthogObserver`).\n\nOne caveat: I could not run the full verifier. `flutter`/`flutter analyze` are blocked from this shell — macOS denies access to `~/development/flutter` (\"Operation not permitted\"), and the standalone Homebrew Dart can't resolve Flutter SDK packages. I verified the files parse cleanly with `dart format` and reviewed types manually, but please run `flutter analyze` where the toolchain is accessible."}
